{"notes": "d1/n24\u2013n35 worker subset, pinned to ea8b12a8a9894b5259c441eadd8f6f0c65e215af. n25: a non-consuming binding can execute and still allow encoding; sequence leader events can also be encoded and held for later flush/drop. n29/n31: ordinary text goes through input.paste.encode; clipboard mode 5522 instead sends a Kitty paste-event MIME listing, not the clipboard text. n33: the guard drops write_small, write_stable and write_alloc at Surface.queueIo; it is not a universal Termio write interlock (e.g. Termio.clearScreen can emit a form feed at a prompt). n35: the actual OS-write scheduling after Exec.write_stream.queueWrite belongs to external libxev, outside the mapped source; the repository connects the stream to the POSIX PTY master or Windows pseudoconsole input pipe. The dedicated validate_source_mappings tool was not exposed to this worker; the subset was checked locally for allowed values, tracked paths, exclusions, bounds, and no duplicated lines within a node."}
